msgid "mail merge"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability to use data from an outside database (or internal "
"database) to <emphasis>personalize</emphasis> your documents for individual "
"members/clients/friends."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the manual will cover all aspects of creating, merging and "
"printing documents that are specific to &kword;. This manual will not cover:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating an external database."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Security issues regarding databases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Detailed instructions on SQL. It is assumed you have some knowledge "
"regarding SQL if you are using a SQL database for your data source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Accessing the network or Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For answers to these questions, other documentation is available on the "
"Internet that is specific to the software you have chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can retreive your mail-merge data from a number of sources:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use an outside SQL database, click <link linkend=\"mail-merge-"
"sql\">here</link> for instructions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use a &kspread; file for your data, click <link linkend="
"\"mail-merge-kspread\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want use information from your &kde; Address Book, click <link "
"linkend=\"mail-merge-ab\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use the internal database of &kword;, click <link linkend="
"\"mail-merge-internal\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using an external SQL database as a data source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "SQL databases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability to use several of the most popular open source "
"databases as a source of data for personalized documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to access an outside database using SQL, your machine needs to have "
"the appropriate database module compiled into your copy of QT."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information see the <link linkend=\"installation\">installation "
"section of this documentation</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The database can be located on the same machine as &kword;, or on any "
"computer which is accessable through your computer network or the Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "In order to use the database, you must know the following information:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name of the database"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Host name/IP address of the computer the database is located on"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "The port address on the specified computer granting SQL access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "A valid user name for the database"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "A valid password for the user name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have all this information at your finger tips, you are ready to "
"proceed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using an outside database to create personalized documents is a three step "
"process:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: mailmerge.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Connect to the database and select your query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"mail-merge-fields\">Insert the merge fields</link> to tell "
"&kword; where to insert the database information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:60 mailmerge.docbook:176 mailmerge.docbook:245
#: mailmerge.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"mail-merge-print\">Print</link> the personalized documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Locate the database and query the records."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:65 mailmerge.docbook:181 mailmerge.docbook:250
#: mailmerge.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To begin, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Mail Merge...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:76 mailmerge.docbook:192 mailmerge.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on <guibutton>Open Existing...</guibutton>. Another small dialog will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>QT-SQL Source</guilabel> and click on <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>. A new dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the &URL; or IP address of the computer that holds the database in the "
"text box labeled <guilabel>Hostname:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the driver named <guilabel>QMYSQL3</guilabel> from the combo box "
"labeled <guilabel>Driver:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the database name you were provided in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Database name:</guilabel> and a user name in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Username:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the database access is through a port other than the default port enter "
"that port number in the text box labeled <guilabel>Port:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are going to be using this database at other times, you can click on "
"the button labeled <guibutton>Keep settings...</guibutton>. &kword; will ask "
"for a descriptive name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you want to restore these settings on future sessions, simply select "
"the descriptive name from the combo box in the upper left of the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When all information is correct, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. &kword; "
"will ask you for a password to that database. Enter the password in the text "
"box, and click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will now ask if you want to replace your current data source with "
"the source you have selected. Click <guibutton>Yes</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are now connected to the database. Now you need to select the data from "
"the database. This dialog box has re-appeared."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on <guibutton>Edit Current...</guibutton>. Another dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog is designed to help you enter and test your database query. The "
"dialog is divided into three sections: Database information, Query "
"information and Query line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The database information section is labeled <guilabel>Information</guilabel> "
"and consists of two combo boxes. The left combo box (<guilabel>Available "
"tables:</guilabel>) gives you a list of all available tables within the "
"current database. Select the desired table from the list by clicking on the "
"table name with the &LMB;. A list of all available fields from that table "
"will appear in the right combo box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The query line is a text box located near the bottom of the dialog labeled "
"<guilabel>Query:</guilabel>. Simply type your SQL query into this text box "
"and click <guibutton>Execute</guibutton>. &kword; will query the database "
"and return the specified query in tabular format in the <guilabel>Query "
"Result</guilabel> box. You can alter, or edit your query on the query line "
"and each time you click <guibutton>Execute</guibutton>, the new query "
"results will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; does not limit your query strings. They can be simple and straight "
"forward:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: mailmerge.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "select * from Clients"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Or complex multitable queries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: mailmerge.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"select Clients.FirstName, Clients.LastName, Clients.address, data.Birthday, "
"data.EyeColour from eMail, data where data.FirstName=Clients.FirstName and "
"data.LastName=Clients.LastName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <guibutton>Setup</guibutton>, will allow you to <link linkend="
"\"mail-merge-login\">log into a different database</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have the correct query in the <guilabel>Query:</guilabel> text box, "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to select that query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will return you to the mail merge main dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:157 mailmerge.docbook:227 mailmerge.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Close</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:159 mailmerge.docbook:229 mailmerge.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that you have selected your data query, it is time to insert the merge "
"fields in the document. Click <link linkend=\"mail-merge-fields\">here to "
"continue</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a &kspread; file as a data source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "using &kspread; file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can use data in a &kspread; document for personalizing documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to use this data, you only need to know the location of the "
"&kspread; document and the worksheet (page) number the data is located on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using a &kspread; document to create personalized documents is a three step "
"process:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: mailmerge.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the file the data is located within."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:174 mailmerge.docbook:243 mailmerge.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"mail-merge-fields\">Insert the merge fields</link> to tell "
"&kword; where to insert the database information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting the file that contains the data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>&kspread; Table Source</guilabel> from the drop down box "
"labeled <guilabel>Available sources:</guilabel> and click on <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>. A new dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the &URL; or file name of the &kspread; document in the text box "
"labeled <guilabel>URL:</guilabel>. You can type the file name directly into "
"the text box, or click on the button with the blue folder and use the file "
"dialog to select the &kspread; file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected the &kspread; document, the drop down box labeled "
"<guilabel>Page number:</guilabel> will show you all the available pages or "
"worksheets within the &kspread; document. Select the page (or worksheet) "
"that contains the mail merge data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When all information is correct, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. &kword; "
"will ask you if you want to replace the current data source. Click "
"<guibutton>Yes</guibutton> to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:218 mailmerge.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "You will again see the mail merge main dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using your &kde; Address book as a data source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "using &kde; Address Book"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; can use data in your address book for personalizing documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using address book entries to create personalized documents is a three step "
"process:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: mailmerge.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the people you want included in the mail merge."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the people you want included"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>&kde; Addressbook Plugin</guilabel> from the drop down box "
"labeled <guilabel>Available sources:</guilabel> and click on <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>. A new dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The dialog consists of two listboxes labeled <guilabel>Address Book</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Selected Addresses</guilabel>. By moving entries "
"from your Address book to the <guilabel>Selected Addresses</guilabel> "
"listbox, you will be including those entries in your merge document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add an entry, select the entry in the left listbox by clicking with the "
"&LMB;. Then click <guibutton>Add</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an entry, select the entry in the right listbox by clicking with "
"the &LMB;. Then click <guibutton>Remove</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can locate entries quickly by entering the first 2-3 letters of an "
"entries name in the textbox labeled <guilabel>Filter on:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can load the full address book application by clicking the "
"<guibutton>Address Book...</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also save a distribution list using the <guibutton>Save as "
"Distribution List...</guibutton> button. For more information on "
"distribution lists, see the documentation on the &kde; Addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have selected all the entries and distribution lists you want, "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. &kword; will ask you if you want to replace "
"the current data source. Click <guibutton>Yes</guibutton> to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using an internal representation of tabular data to create documents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "using &kword; data tables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For small sets of data, or when you do not currently have a database "
"containing the merge data, &kword; offers you the ability to enter the data "
"<emphasis>directly into &kword;</emphasis> in tabular form. This internal "
"data structure can then be used to create documents with this data inserted "
"at predefined locations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using an internal representation of the data to create personalized "
"documents is a three step process:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"mail-merge-internal-data\">Enter the data</link> into &kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the data has been created once, you can go back and change the data as "
"needed, and produce another set of personalized documents from that data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on <guibutton>Create New...</guibutton>. Another small dialog will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is currently only one option in this dialog box <guilabel>Internal "
"Storage</guilabel>. Click on <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. A new dialog box "
"will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a record card for creating your tabular data file. Along the top is "
"a toolbar and the main part of the dialog is space to hold your entry/data "
"pairs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining the structure of your data table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, we need to add one or more entries (merge fields). This is "
"accomplished by clicking the <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"addentry.png\" format=\"PNG\" align=\"center\"/></imageobject></"
"inlinemediaobject> (<guilabel>Add entry</guilabel>) button (third button "
"from the right along the toolbar). A small dialog box will appear. Type a "
"descriptive name of your entry in the dialog box (Name, Address, Balance "
"Due, etc....)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is for the name of the entry, not the data that is contained within the "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>, and the entry is added to the card."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Repeat this process until all needed entries are visible on this first card."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to delete an entry, simply click once on the entry name with the "
"&LMB; and select <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"delentry.png\" format=\"PNG\" align=\"center\"/></imageobject></"
"inlinemediaobject> (<guilabel>Remove entry</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be <emphasis>very</emphasis> sure you have selected the correct entry name. "
"Once you tell &kword; to delete the entry, the entry <emphasis>and all of "
"the data within those entries will be deleted immediately</emphasis>. You "
"will not be given the option to stop or reverse the process once it is begun."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Entering the data into the table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that the structure of your data is defined, you can enter the data into "
"your entries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the top of the dialog box, are 4 buttons surrounding a spin box. The spin "
"box gives the current record number. All records are numbered in the order "
"they are added starting with number 1. You can use the spin box to go "
"directly to the desired record or you can use the arrows to graphically move "
"through the list of records."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Button"
msgstr "Boton"

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Action"
msgstr "Accion"

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move directly to record one"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move back one record"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move forward one record"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mailmerge.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move to the last record in the dataset"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enter the data, simply place the cursor in the text box to the right of "
"the entry name, and type in the data. (&kword; uses <quote>No Value</quote> "
"as the default value for all entries in newly created records.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a record, click the <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"addrecord.png\" format=\"PNG\" align=\"center\"/></imageobject></"
"inlinemediaobject> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a record, click the <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"delrecord.png\" format=\"PNG\" align=\"center\"/></imageobject></"
"inlinemediaobject> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be careful when you are deleting records. Once deleted, the record cannot be "
"retrieved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Continue to enter all data until your dataset is complete."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After your dataset is complete, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save the "
"changes to your dataset. This will bring up the mail merge main dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Close</guibutton>. Now it is time to insert the merge "
"fields in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert merge fields in document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that &kword; knows the entries available in your data source, you can "
"insert the merge fields into your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A merge field is a placeholder within the document. This placeholder will be "
"replaced in each personalized document with the value of the entry for that "
"individual record."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a merge field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "inserting merge fields"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a merge field, place the cursor at the desired place in the "
"document. Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Variable</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Mail Merge...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A list of available entries will "
"appear. Select the desired entry, and click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The merge field is inserted at the current cursor location. The merge field "
"is surrounded by brackets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can place the cursor in a new location in the document and insert "
"another placeholder. When you are done inserting placeholders, you can "
"proceed to printing your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete a merge field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting a merge field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can delete a merge field two ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the cursor at the end of the merge field, and press the &Backspace; "
"key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the cursor at the beginning of the merge field, and press the "
"<keycap>Delete</keycap> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Previewing and printing the merged document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mailmerge.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "merging data and text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have inserted all the merge fields you want, you are ready to "
"preview and print the personalized documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preview your documents before printing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To preview your document select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Mail Merge...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guilabel>Print Preview...</guilabel>. You will be able to see the "
"final output of your personalized documents prior to printing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mailmerge.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "Print your personalized documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mailmerge.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You print personalized documents using the same methods that you do to print "
"traditional documents. For more information on printing see the section on "
"<link linkend=\"printing\">Printing a Document</link>."
msgstr ""
